# Chapter 1 — In the Beginning, God Created

> *"In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth."* — Genesis 1:1 (ESV)

---

## §1. The Question I Was Handed at the Kitchen Table

It was late. Past ten. The kind of late where the coffee pot has been emptied twice and the dogs have surrendered to their beds in the corner.

My wife and I were at the kitchen table. Legal pad. Bible open. A passage from a homeschool friend's recent conversation with her son sitting between us like a third chair at the table.

*"Dad, my friend at co-op said the Bible is a myth. She said her dad told her that real scientists don't believe Genesis. That it's just an old story people used to tell before they knew better. Is that true?"*

If you are a Christian parent, you have had some version of this conversation. Maybe it came from your own child. Maybe from a niece or a grandson. Maybe from a Sunday-school class you walked into on a Wednesday night because the youth pastor was out of town and there were twelve middle-schoolers who had questions. Maybe from yourself, quietly, in a car on the way home from an astrophysics documentary that your husband loved and you couldn't bring yourself to say why it had made you feel small.

I want to say something to you before we go any further, because you deserve to hear it before this book spends 60,000 words making its case.

*You have not been wrong to trust your Bible. And you do not have to choose.*

I am an aerospace engineer. I earned my degree at Embry-Riddle, commissioned into the Air Force, and spent five years wearing a uniform — including a tour at the National Reconnaissance Office, which is the agency that operates our country's reconnaissance satellites, and a deployment to Iraq during the transition. After active duty I went to Boeing's unmanned aerial subsidiary for nine years, where I pioneered agile development for combined hardware and software teams, and the FAA certification process for unmanned aircraft. I co-founded a company that NASA designated a spinoff. I am writing this from my homestead in the Columbia River Gorge with cows and a mule in the back pasture and an RF test bench in the shop.

I tell you all of that not to brag. I tell you because the question your child asked deserves an answer from someone who has, in the phrase engineers use when we don't know yet whether something will fly, *earned his flight hours.* I have earned mine. The people who told your child that real scientists have outgrown Genesis do not know what they are talking about. I am going to show you, over the course of this book, that the first chapter of your Bible is not a pre-scientific myth.

It is a *specification.*

And the specification matches.

